'#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Taekwondo in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/TKW'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Taekwondo at the 2024 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "7 – 10 August 2024"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2167"} "Grand Palais, Paris, France"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The taekwondo competitions at the 2024 Summer Olympics in Paris ran from 7-10 August, at the " [:a {:href "/venues/2167"} "Grand Palais"] " strip. A total of 128 fighters, with an equal distribution between men and women, competed across eight different weight categories (four per gender), the same amount as at all editions since Beijing 2008. Each weight category was composed of sixteen fighters; however, this figure could increase if additional athletes were invited and selected from the Refugee Olympic Team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Only one country, South Korea, won two gold medals, and six countries won more than one medal. For South Korea, these were rehabilitation Games. They did not win a single gold medal in Tokyo, which was seen as a major failure, but two gold medals in the first two days of competition in Paris made this a memorable Olympics for the Koreans.\nIran was another country that improved on its Tokyo 2020 results. They had won taekwondo medals at every Olympic Games, but failed to win any in Tokyo. In Paris, they won four, which was the country’s best result since taekwondo became an Olympic sport. On the final day of competition, " [:a {:href "/athletes/155014"} "Arian Salimi"] " won gold and helped Iran finish second in the medal table."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Belgium and Hungary won their very first taekwondo Olympic medals, with Hungary’s medal being gold. " [:a {:href "/athletes/131834"} "Panipak Wongpattanakit"] " of Thailand and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504275"} "Ulugbek Rashitov"] " of Uzbekistan won gold in Tokyo and successfully retained their titles in Paris."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130586"} "Kimia Alizadeh"] " competed in her third Olympics and won her second bronze medal. The former Iranian athlete, who won Iran’s first medal in women’s taekwondo at Rio 2016, represented the Refugee Olympic Team in Tokyo. She began representing Bulgaria in 2024, however, and won her second bronze medal for the country."] "\n\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2007550"} "Flyweight (≤58 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} " 7 August 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/2007575"} "Featherweight (≤68 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} " 8 August 2024"] "\n" [:td {} "17"]